under the United States Constitution  Congress makes the laws and the  president enforces the laws a law  provides Authority for the president and  the agencies of the government to compel  individuals corporations and others to  take or not to take certain acts for  example a law authorizes the President  to collect taxes through the Internal  Revenue Service neither the president  nor the IRS can collect taxes or do  anything else without a supporting law  from Congress however the laws leave the  IRS and other agencies with discretion  on how they enforce the law an executive  order is the president's written  direction to the agencies of the  government about how he wants them to  act when they enforce the law for  example President Trump issued an  executive order directing all agencies  to eliminate two regulations for every  regulation the issue as long as the  order is consistent with the  Constitution and the law the president  can use an executive order to tell the  IRS and others how he wants them to do  what Congress has authorized our  executive orders by President Trump a  good idea let us know in your comments  and also let us know what other topics  you want a EEI scholars to cover in 60  seconds
 

